.TH FIGLET-FONT-PREVIEW 1 "November 15, 2026"
.SH NAME
figlet-font-preview \- preview text in every installed FIGlet and TOIlet font
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B figlet-font-preview
.RB [ \-\-center " | " \-\-right ]
.RB [ \-\-font\-dir
.IR DIR ]...
.RI [ text ]
.br
.B figlet-font-preview
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B figlet-font-preview
is an interactive terminal program.
It renders a sample text in every FIGlet and TOIlet font it finds,
with a fuzzy-searchable, multi-select font sidebar
for comparing fonts side by side.
.PP
The program parses and renders the font files itself.
It never runs
.BR figlet (6),
so only the font files need to be installed.
.PP
The remaining arguments are joined with spaces to form the initial text.
The default is
.BR Hello .
.SH OPTIONS
Options may be given with one or two leading dashes, for example
.B \-center
or
.BR \-\-center .
.TP
.B \-\-center
Centre the rendered text in the preview.
.TP
.B \-\-right
Right-align the rendered text in the preview.
The default is left; when several of these flags are given, the last one wins.
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-dir " DIR"
Also search
.I DIR
for fonts.
May be repeated.
.B \-\-font\-dir=\c
.I DIR
is accepted too.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
On a terminal, print a "FIGLET FONT PREVIEW" banner centred to the terminal width, with the version beneath.
The font is AMC AAA01 when it is installed and fits, otherwise the widest built\-in FIGlet font that fits (banner, small, mini).
When even mini does not fit (below 23 columns), or output is not a terminal, print only the version line.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage text, including the default font roots, and exit.
.SH KEYS
.SS Anywhere
.TP
.B tab\fR, \fBshift+tab
Cycle focus: Text, Fonts (landing on the list), Filters and the Style pane while it is open.
While the Fonts pane is hidden, only the text and the Style pane take focus.
The focused pane has an accent outline.
.TP
.B ctrl+e
Focus the text.
.TP
.B ctrl+f
Focus the search.
When Style has hidden the Fonts pane, Style closes first.
.TP
.B ctrl+t
Focus the filters, with the same rule.
.TP
.B ctrl+k
Open the command palette: every action with its key, filtered as you type.
.B up
and
.B down
move,
.B enter
runs the action, and
.B esc
or
.B ctrl+k
closes it.
Any other app key, such as
.B ctrl+e
or
.BR ctrl+c ,
closes the palette and does its job.
.TP
.B ?
Open the help screen: the cursor and pick legend first, then every action with its key and the keys of each pane. The bottom edge of the box shows "more" with a down arrow while there is more below.
It opens everywhere except the text and the search, where
.B ?
types a question mark.
.BR up ", " down ", " j ", " k ", " pgup " and " pgdn
scroll it, and
.B esc
or
.B ?
closes it.
Other app keys close it and do their job.
.TP
.BR pgup ", " pgdn ", " ctrl+u ", " ctrl+d ", mouse wheel"
Scroll the preview.
.TP
.B ctrl+o
Show or hide the Style pane.
Below 79 columns the Fonts pane steps aside while Style is open and returns when it closes.
Below 47 columns Style does not open.
.TP
.B ctrl+y
Copy the cursor font's render to the clipboard as plain text,
wrapped and aligned as shown.
.TP
.B ctrl+s
Save the cursor font's render as a coloured
.IB font .svg
in the current directory.
An existing file is never overwritten; \-2, \-3, ... is added to the name.
.TP
.B ctrl+c
Quit.
.B esc
and
.B q
never quit.
.SS Text
.TP
.BR "type" ", " enter
Edit the text.
.B enter
starts a new line.
.BR ctrl+e ", " ctrl+f ", " ctrl+t " and " ctrl+k
are app keys here, so
.B end
and
.B right
do the line-editing jobs.
.TP
.B esc
Go to the Fonts list.
.SS Search
.TP
.B type
Fuzzy-filter fonts.
.TP
.BR up ", " down
Move in the list.
.TP
.B enter
Go to the list, keeping the query.
.TP
.B esc
Clear the search and go to the list.
.SS List
.TP
.BR up ", " down ", " j ", " k ", " g ", " G
Move.
.TP
.BR space ", " enter
Select or deselect.
.TP
.B x
Clear the selection.
.TP
.B /
Jump to the search.
.TP
.B esc
Clear the search.
.SS Filters
The filter checklist, in its own frame below the Fonts pane.
.TP
.BR up ", " down ", " j ", " k
Move.
.TP
.BR space ", " enter ", " right ", " l
Toggle the row, or step Group by forward.
.TP
.BR left ", " h
Step Group by back.
.TP
.B esc
Back to the list.
.SS Style pane
.TP
.BR up ", " down ", " j ", " k
Move.
.TP
.BR space ", " enter
Change the row.
.TP
.BR left ", " right ", " h ", " l
Change Align, the background Mode, or a slider's value.
.TP
.B esc
Go to the Fonts list, leaving the pane open.
Below 79 columns Style closes so the Fonts pane can show.
.TP
.B ctrl+o
Close the pane.
.SH FILES
Fonts are read from these directories when they exist:
.RS
.nf
/opt/homebrew/share/figlet
/usr/local/share/figlet
/usr/share/figlet
~/figlet-fonts
.fi
.RE
.PP
On Windows only
.B %USERPROFILE%\efiglet-fonts
and the
.B \-\-font\-dir
directories are searched.
Fonts in different directories are listed separately
even when they are the same font.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR figlet (6),
.BR toilet (1)
